YANI: equal rights for the bugs on the floor.

Right now, "the bugs on the floor" exist only as
dungeon dressing, as parts of some engrave testing
messages. Is this fair? Of course it isn't!  Let's
have equal rights for the bugs on the floor!

When the PC engrave tests a wand and gets a "the
bugs on the floor" ... "yadda yadda" message, that
should create one or more likely several monsters of
the same type summoned by priests with their "summon
insects" spell, slowed, hastened, asleep, or corpses
as appropriate, surrounding the PC at an at least
two grid cells displacement to permit some reaction
time for the PC.

This would put a bit of spice in the process of
engrave testing, which is now a bit _too_ safe, with
only "create monster" and "lightning" bein real
issues.

This would _also_ enrich the supply of monsters for
altar camping sac fests, as an _intended_ side
effect, and give alternate uses for popcorn wands
that aren't otherwise always all that useful once
IDed.

Also, it would better differentiate the results of
engrave testing a wand of sleep versus a wand of
death.

Quantum valeat.

